---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CRITERIA } from '../lib/convention';
---
<Base title="Method" current="about" description="How easeprint measures a site, what the words mean, and what it can't see.">
  <article class="wrap method">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1 class="display">Method</h1>
      <p class="lede">Each number here was read from a browser while it visited the site. Nothing was estimated from video or copied from a stylesheet by eye.</p>
    </header>

    <section aria-labelledby="visit">
      <h2 class="h2" id="visit">One visit</h2>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><strong>Load once</strong> in Chromium at 1440 by 900, wait for the network to settle, then three more seconds.</li>
        <li><strong>Scroll</strong> to the bottom with the mouse wheel, in steps of 80% of the viewport, pausing 450ms each.</li>
        <li><strong>Hover and leave</strong> up to 30 distinct links and buttons, spread through the page.</li>
        <li><strong>Click</strong>, only for component demo sites whose motion needs it (Sonner, Vaul): their own demo buttons, then Escape. Listed in the raw file.</li>
        <li><strong>Scan</strong> every element's computed <code>transition</code> and <code>animation</code>, including <code>::before</code> and <code>::after</code>.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        Throughout, a probe injected before the page's own scripts records every <code>transitionrun</code> and
        <code>animationstart</code> event with the exact computed timing, every <code>element.animate()</code> call,
        <code>document.getAnimations()</code> every 120ms, and GSAP's timeline when a page exposes it. Stylesheet and
        script text is scanned for counts only (reduced-motion queries, <code>transition: all</code>, keyframe names,
        library fingerprints). No site code, asset or screenshot is stored.
      </p>
      <p>
        A second run does the same with <code>prefers-reduced-motion: reduce</code>. Each run is one load. Raw files
        are published beside the site, and an entry's values must match one raw record exactly (timing, duration,
        phase, property, selector, count) or the build fails.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="words">
      <h2 class="h2" id="words">Words</h2>
      <dl class="glossary">
        <div><dt>Spatial</dt><dd>Motion that says where things are and where they go: travel, slides, layers, stacks.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Material</dt><dd>Motion that says what things are made of: press, give, glow, blur, spring.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Ambient</dt><dd>Motion that runs on its own, not in answer to you. <em>Decorative</em> (marquees, drifts), <em>diagrammatic</em> (product diagrams that explain), or <em>character</em> (motion with a personality).</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Statement</dt><dd>The one big move. At most one per site here.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Secondary</dt><dd>Long moves under the statement.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Signature</dt><dd>The move that's recognisably theirs, often an overshoot.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Utility</dt><dd>Hover, press, colour: the fast floor.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Exit</dt><dd>Leaving, when it's timed differently from arriving.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="verdicts">
      <h2 class="h2" id="verdicts">Reduced motion verdicts</h2>
      <p>Movement events (transform, translate, scale, rotate, position, size) in the reduced run as a share of the normal run. Fades are allowed under reduced motion, so they don't count against a site.</p>
      <dl class="glossary">
        <div><dt>Honored</dt><dd>20% or less of the movement remains.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Partly honored</dt><dd>More than 20%, up to 75%.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Not honored</dt><dd>More than 75% remains.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Nothing measured moves</dt><dd>No movement in the normal run, so nothing to reduce in CSS or WAAPI.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="limits">
      <h2 class="h2" id="limits">What it can't see</h2>
      <ul class="limits">
        <li>Motion run on <code>requestAnimationFrame</code>: smooth scroll (Lenis, Locomotive), GSAP tweens on pages that don't expose GSAP, Framer Motion springs not handed to WAAPI.</li>
        <li>Anything drawn in a canvas. Entries say "motion lives in canvas" when a WebGL canvas covers a quarter of the viewport or more.</li>
        <li>Menus, forms, drags, other pages, and states behind clicks (except the two demo sites).</li>
        <li>Timing only. Distances, scale amounts and keyframe values aren't recorded, so the demos show each curve as a fixed travel or a fade.</li>
        <li>One visit on one day. Sites change; a measurement is true for its date.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="convention-def">
      <h2 class="h2" id="convention-def">The convention, as tests</h2>
      <p>An aggressive ease-out (at least {CRITERIA.minProgressAtQuarter * 100}% of the distance by 25% of the time), {CRITERIA.minStatementMs}ms or longer, with a non-ambient tier of {CRITERIA.maxFastMs}ms or less on the same site. <a href="/convention/">See who passes.</a></p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="run">
      <h2 class="h2" id="run">Run it</h2>
      <pre class="value"><code>pnpm measure https://example.com
pnpm measure https://example.com --reduced
pnpm summarize data/raw/example.com/2026-10-17.json</code></pre>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-head {
    padding-block: var(--s8) var(--s5);
  }

  .page-head .lede {
    margin-top: var(--s4);
  }

  .method section {
    max-width: 46em;
    margin-top: var(--s7);
  }

  .method section > p {
    margin-top: var(--s3);
  }

  .steps,
  .limits {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s2);
    margin-top: var(--s4);
    padding-left: 1.4em;
  }

  .steps {
    list-style: decimal;
  }

  .limits {
    list-style: disc;
  }

  .glossary {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s3);
    margin-top: var(--s4);
  }

  .glossary div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 11em 1fr;
    gap: var(--s4);
    padding-top: var(--s3);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  @media (width <= 560px) {
    .glossary div {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--s1);
    }
  }

  .glossary dt {
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .glossary dd {
    margin: 0;
  }

  pre {
    margin-top: var(--s4);
    padding: var(--s4);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--r);
    background: var(--canvas);
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
</style>
